`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"renamed-va-events",children:"Renamed VA events"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.code,{children:"va.role.update"})," becomes ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"va.crl-settings.update"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"va.role.crl.init"})," becomes ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"va.crl-settings.init"}),"; ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"va.role.crl.create"})," keeps its name and its payload. Every subject changes from ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"crl/<ski>"})," to ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"crl/<ca-id>"}),", and the payload of the renamed events changes from the old VA role to the CRL settings of the CA, with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ca_id"})," instead of ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ca_ski"}),". The alerts migration renames the event types of existing subscriptions automatically, but it does not rewrite their conditions — JSON Path, JSON Schema or JavaScript: review conditions that filter on the old payload or on the old ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"crl/<ski>"})," subject, including those for ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"va.role.crl.create"}),". Direct event-bus consumers and audit searches must adopt the new names and payload themselves."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"enrollment-behavior",children:"Enrollment behavior"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h4,{id:"fail-closed-revocation-checks",children:"Fail-closed revocation checks"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Enrollment and re-enrollment now verify the revocation of the presented certificates and fail closed when it cannot be verified. There is no migration: every pre-existing DMS has the new ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"allow_unverifiable_revocation"})," option at its default ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"false"}),", so a certificate that is not managed by Lamassu and carries no OCSP or CRL distribution points is rejected until the option is set to ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"true"})," in the affected block, independently for the enrollment and the re-enrollment block."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Certificates that do carry endpoints are still strictly checked: unreachable endpoints, stale or inconclusive answers reject the certificate even when ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"allow_unverifiable_revocation"})," is enabled, and certificates managed by Lamassu are unaffected because their stored status is used. A validation CA revoked in Lamassu also rejects the operation, without falling back to the remaining validation CAs. See the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/est/configuration#authentication-per-operation",children:"DMS guide"})," and ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/est/bootstrap-identity#revocation-and-checks",children:"Revocation and checks"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{id:"helm-migration-guide",children:"Helm migration guide"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The upgrade runs in a fixed order: prepare the data and values, run ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"helm upgrade"}),", then copy the KMS and VA data into the new volumes. The copy must run after the upgrade, because the destination StatefulSets and PVCs do not exist before it. If you are not upgrading an existing release, go straight to ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm",children:"Install with Helm"}),"."]}),`
