`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Without the chart's database job, no tool moves data between databases: the migration tooling only applies migrations to a schema that already exists. Move each per-service database into its ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"pki"})," schema yourself, preserving structure, indexes, constraints, data and migration history, with writes stopped and a verified backup in hand."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Run the migrations in the required order, one schema at a time: ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"kms"})," first, then the ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ca-to-kms-migration"})," tool (needed only for legacy deployments whose CA keys are named by SKI), then ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ca"}),", then ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"va"}),". The ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"devicemanager"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"dmsmanager"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"alerts"})," schemas are independent and can be migrated in any order. With Helm, the chart's pre-install job applies the schemas in the correct order automatically."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["If ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"kms"})," has not been migrated, the ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ca"})," migration fails with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"kms schema not found: migrate the kms schema before the ca schema"}),". The ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"va"})," migration requires ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ca"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"kms"})," to be migrated first: it fails with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ca schema not found: migrate the ca schema before the va schema"})," or ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"kms schema not found: migrate the kms schema before the va schema"})," if one of them is missing."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The schemas reference each other, so the PostgreSQL role running the migrations needs cross-schema privileges: the ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ca"})," schema needs ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"USAGE"})," on ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"kms"})," plus ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"SELECT"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"REFERENCES"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"INSERT"})," on ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"kms.kms_keys"}),", and the ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"va"})," schema needs ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"USAGE"})," on ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ca"})," plus ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"SELECT"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"REFERENCES"})," on ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ca.certificates"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"SELECT"})," on ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ca.ca_certificates"}),", and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"USAGE"})," on ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"kms"})," plus ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"SELECT"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"REFERENCES"})," on ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"kms.kms_keys"}),". Without them the migration aborts; grant the missing privileges and rerun the failed schema. After migrating ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ca"}),", if the CA service runs as a different user than the migration user, grant it ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"SELECT"})," on ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ca.certificates_view"})," (",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"GRANT SELECT ON ca.certificates_view TO service_user"}),"). Without this grant, certificate and CA reads fail with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"permission denied for table certificates_view"}),". After migrating ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"va"}),", if the CA service runs as a different user, grant it ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"USAGE"})," on the ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"va"})," schema and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"SELECT"})," on ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"va.crl_settings"})," (",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA va TO service_user; GRANT SELECT ON va.crl_settings TO service_user"}),"): the CA service reads ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"va.crl_settings"})," when it deletes a CA, and without these grants every deletion of a CA that has a crypto engine fails with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"permission denied for schema va"})," (or ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"for table crl_settings"}),")."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["To apply migrations by hand, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"goose-lamassu"})," must run against the ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"pki"})," database with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"search_path=<schema>"})," in the connection string. The binary validates only ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"search_path"}),", not the database name, so check ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"dbname=pki"})," before running it, and repeat for ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"kms"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ca"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"va"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"devicemanager"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"dmsmanager"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"alerts"}),":"]}),`
